\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $AB=BA={I}_{2}$\n- **II.** $AC=CA={I}_{2}$\n- **III.** $C\\ne {A}^{-1}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $BA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & -3 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false. As a result, $C\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement III is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237921 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "caf47f24-5826-503b-9314-2ce4fcb361ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461213} {:answer/id #uuid "66e828c3-1224-5037-bfe0-efa2537a90f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461214}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461213} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b58693c-bbc8-5575-a394-e3f95bcc8188" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 1759